A **data-retention fault** (DRF) shows only after the cell has been left alone for a while. March notation adds a **Del** element — a pause with no access:

> {⇕(w0); Del; ⇕(r0, w1); Del; ⇕(r1)}

The pause is typically tens to hundreds of milliseconds, often at **high temperature** and **low supply voltage**, where leakage is worst.
